{
  "provider": {
    "version": 0,
    "block": {
      "attributes": {
        "api_token": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "The API token to use for authentication. Defaults to `METAL_STACK_CLOUD_API_TOKEN`.",
          "description_kind": "markdown",
          "optional": true,
          "sensitive": true
        },
        "project": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "The project to use for authentication. Defaults to `METAL_STACK_CLOUD_PROJECT` or derived from `api_token`.",
          "description_kind": "markdown",
          "optional": true
        }
      },
      "description": "Manage bare-metal Kubernetes clusters on [metalstack.cloud](https://metalstack.cloud).\n\nTo obtain an `api token` for creating resources, visit [metalstack.cloud](https://metalstack.cloud). Head to the the `Access Tokens` section and create a new one with the desired permissions, name and validity. \n**Note:** Watch out to first select the desired organization and project you want the token to be valid for. \n\nAll provider defaults can be derived from the environment variables `METAL_STACK_CLOUD_*` or set in the terraform provider configuration.",
      "description_kind": "markdown"
    }
  },
  "resource_schemas": {
    "metal_cluster": {
      "version": 0,
      "block": {
        "attributes": {
          "created_at": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Creation timestamp of the cluster",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "ID of the cluster",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "kubernetes": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Only newer versions can be specified. There is no downgrade possibility.\n\t\t\tPlease be aware that it is not possible to skip major and minor updates.\n\t\t\tIt is only possible to upgrade in order. For example from 1.23.3 to 1.24.0, not to 1.25.0.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "required": true
          },
          "maintenance": {
            "nested_type": {
              "attributes": {
                "kubernetes_autoupdate": {
                  "type": "bool",
                  "description": "Whether kubernetes autoupdate is enabled",
                  "description_kind": "markdown",
                  "computed": true
                },
                "machineimage_autoupdate": {
                  "type": "bool",
                  "description": "Whether machine image autoupdate is enabled",
                  "description_kind": "markdown",
                  "computed": true
                },
                "time_window": {
                  "nested_type": {
                    "attributes": {
                      "begin": {
                        "nested_type": {
                          "attributes": {
                            "hour": {
                              "type": "number",
                              "description": "Hour of the maintenance window",
                              "description_kind": "plain",
                              "required": true
                            },
                            "minute": {
                              "type": "number",
                              "description": "Minute of the maintenance window",
                              "description_kind": "plain",
                              "required": true
                            },
                            "time_zone": {
                              "type": "string",
                              "description": "Timezone of the maintenance window. The timezone will be `UTC` and set automatically",
                              "description_kind": "plain",
                              "computed": true
                            }
                          },
                          "nesting_mode": "single"
                        },
                        "description": "Begin of the maintenance window",
                        "description_kind": "plain",
                        "required": true
                      },
                      "duration": {
                        "type": "number",
                        "description": "Set duration of maintenance window. The duration must be defined in hours.",
                        "description_kind": "markdown",
                        "required": true
                      }
                    },
                    "nesting_mode": "single"
                  },
                  "description": "Set time window for maintenance",
                  "description_kind": "markdown",
                  "required": true
                }
              },
              "nesting_mode": "single"
            },
            "description": "maintenance options",
            "description_kind": "markdown",
            "required": true
          },
          "name": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "This is the name of the cluster that will be used to identify it. It can not be changed afterwards.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "required": true
          },
          "partition": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Partition ID",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "optional": true,
            "computed": true
          },
          "project": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Project ID",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "optional": true,
            "computed": true
          },
          "tenant": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Tenant ID",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "optional": true,
            "computed": true
          },
          "updated_at": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Update timestamp of the cluster",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "workers": {
            "nested_type": {
              "attributes": {
                "machine_type": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "The machine type for this worker group",
                  "description_kind": "markdown",
                  "required": true
                },
                "max_size": {
                  "type": "number",
                  "description": "The maximum count of available nodes with type machinetype for autoscaling",
                  "description_kind": "markdown",
                  "required": true
                },
                "max_surge": {
                  "type": "number",
                  "description": "The maximum count of available nodes which can be updated at once",
                  "description_kind": "markdown",
                  "optional": true,
                  "computed": true
                },
                "max_unavailable": {
                  "type": "number",
                  "description": "The maximum count of nodes which can be unavailable during node updates",
                  "description_kind": "markdown",
                  "optional": true,
                  "computed": true
                },
                "min_size": {
                  "type": "number",
                  "description": "The minimum count of available nodes with type machinetype",
                  "description_kind": "markdown",
                  "required": true
                },
                "name": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "The group name of the worker nodes",
                  "description_kind": "markdown",
                  "required": true
                }
              },
              "nesting_mode": "list"
            },
            "description": "Choose the type of server best suited for your cluster.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "required": true
          }
        },
        "description": "Managing Clusters of worker nodes. Required permissions: `Cluster *`. Can be imported by ID or name.",
        "description_kind": "markdown"
      }
    },
    "metal_public_ip": {
      "version": 0,
      "block": {
        "attributes": {
          "created_at": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Indicates when this IP address has initially been claimed.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "description": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Here you can give your IP an optional description for your own use.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "optional": true,
            "computed": true
          },
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The ID that represents this public IP address.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "ip": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The publicly accessible IP address.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "name": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "You can give your IP address a freely chosen name to identify it in the future.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "required": true
          },
          "network": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The network this address is bound to.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "project": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The project this address is part of. Cannot be moved.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "tags": {
            "type": [
              "list",
              "string"
            ],
            "description": "The tags used to organize this address.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          },
          "type": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Determines the type of the public ip address. \n\tIf you want the IP to outlive the cluster lifecycle, mark it as static. Otherwise it will be deleted along with the cluster. \n\tAnother use case would be if you want to have a stable egress address on the internet gateway for your cluster.\n\tMust be either 'static' or 'ephemeral'. Static IPs cannot be made ephemeral.\n\t\t\t",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "optional": true,
            "computed": true
          },
          "updated_at": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Indicates when this IP address has been updated.",
            "description_kind": "plain",
            "computed": true
          }
        },
        "description": "Each cluster gets an IP automatically provided on the internet gateway for outgoing communication. \nServices get an IP automatically on creation. \nServices and gateway IPs are dynamic by default. \nYou can use an IP address in several clusters and locations at the same time. \nRequired permissions: `IP *`. Can be imported by ID, name or ip address.",
        "description_kind": "markdown"
      }
    }
  },
